# Bot1's Leyline of the Void: "If a card would be put into an opponent's graveyard from anywhere, exile it instead" (CR 614).
# Bot1's Lightning Bolt kills Bot2's Doomed Traveler, but the Traveler is exiled in place of going to the graveyard, so it never
# dies (CR 700.4) and its trigger does not happen: Bot2 has no Spirit and an empty graveyard. The only thing that keeps the
# Spirit away is the replacement (the Bolt alone, in doomed-traveler-dying-to-a-bolt..., leaves one).

[Bot1 Deck]
Leyline of the Void
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x4
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Doomed Traveler
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Doomed Traveler.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Doomed Traveler)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Exile = Doomed Traveler
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Pearl
Bot1.Battlefield = Leyline of the Void; Mox Ruby
